Feature: sdtrd installer for OpenSpec projects
  As a team running OpenSpec
  We want "sdtrd" to wire itself into an existing openspec/ project
  So that SDTRD gates, hooks and CI are added without disturbing OpenSpec.

  Scenario: Fresh install (4.1, REQ-OSA-11, 12)
    Given a repo initialized with "openspec init" and OpenSpec >= 1.15.0
    When the installer runs
    Then "openspec/schemas/sdtrd/schema.yaml" exists
    And "openspec/config.yaml" has "schema: sdtrd"
    And the pre-commit config, CI workflow, mutation templates, branch-protection hook and agent rules are present
    And ".gitignore" contains ".worktrees/"

  Scenario: Idempotent re-run (4.2, REQ-OSA-13)
    Given a completed install
    When the installer runs again
    Then no file changes
    And the exit code is 0

  Scenario: Missing prerequisite (4.3, REQ-OSA-11)
    Given a directory without "openspec/"
    When the installer runs
    Then it exits non-zero with a message
    And nothing is written

  Scenario: Old or absent OpenSpec CLI (REQ-OSA-11)
    Given "openspec" is missing from PATH or reports a version below 1.15.0
    When the installer runs
    Then it exits non-zero naming the required version
    And nothing is written

  Scenario: Config preservation (4.4, REQ-OSA-14)
    Given "openspec/config.yaml" with "context" and "rules" keys
    When the installer runs
    Then those keys are unchanged
    And "schema: sdtrd" is set

  Scenario: Existing pre-commit config is kept (REQ-OSA-14)
    Given a user ".pre-commit-config.yaml"
    When the installer runs
    Then that file is byte-identical afterwards

  Scenario: Another schema already set (Edge 1)
    Given "openspec/config.yaml" with "schema: spec-driven"
    When the installer runs
    Then "schema: sdtrd" is set
    And the previous value "spec-driven" is printed

  Scenario: No config.yaml (Edge 2)
    Given "openspec/" without "config.yaml"
    When the installer runs
    Then "openspec/config.yaml" is created containing only "schema: sdtrd"

  Scenario: Target is not a git repository (Edge 3)
    Given an OpenSpec project that is not a git repository
    When the installer runs
    Then hooks are skipped with a warning
    And schema and config wiring still occur
    And the exit code is 0

  Scenario: Rules survive "openspec update" (REQ-OSA-15)
    Given a completed install
    Then SDTRD rules live outside files regenerated by "openspec update"
